# Git commits

- **Never** create commits yourself (`git commit`, `git add` + commit, etc.).
- When changes are ready to commit, **always** provide the exact command(s) for the user to run.
- Do not ask whether to commit first — just supply the command after finishing the work.
- Follow the repo’s existing commit-message style when drafting the message.
